#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186153437 :tutorial/content "Recall that two variables, $x$ and $y$, are said to have a proportional relationship if their ratio is constant. The constant of proportionality $k$ is given by\n\n$$\nk = \\dfrac{y}{x}\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the equation above as follows:\n\n$$\ny = kx\n$$\n\nThe following statements are all equivalent:\n\n- $y = kx$\n- $y$ **varies directly** with $x$\n- $y$ is **directly proportional** to $x$\n- $y \\propto x$\n\nProportional relationships frequently occur in real-world problems. Let's see an example." :tutorial/id #uuid "cd20b689-18a3-54cb-97a9-7fa52d610ec1" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8191 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
